# Units tsOS keeps disabled. On the first boot (/etc/machine-id "uninitialized"), systemd applies
# the presets to every unit, and Debian's policy enables whatever no preset names. That enabled
# these next to the units the image is built with. Only first matches count, so this file wins
# over 90-systemd.preset. Units the build enables are not listed: "disable *" would turn them off.

# Debian's alternative to caddy.service, for a server configured only through the admin API
# (--resume). Both bind 80 and 443; whichever starts first wins.
disable caddy-api.service

# NetworkManager manages the network; systemd-networkd would leave every link unmanaged.
disable systemd-networkd.service
disable systemd-networkd.socket
disable systemd-network-generator.service

# Raspberry Pi OS's USB gadget sharing switches usb0, which is the ECM interface of some LTE
# modems here (70-quectel-ec200a-nm-unmanaged.rules).
disable rpi-usb-gadget-ics.service

# Debian's firewall loader: an empty accept-all ruleset after `flush ruleset`. Not configured.
disable nftables.service

# The rsync daemon; not used.
disable rsync.service
